# hsb: half-open polyhedra.
#
# See demos/README.md for how to run this script.

# An hsb constant is a set of points given by half-spaces over the coordinates
# x[0], x[1], ... The two extremes are bot and top:

{top}:hsb
{bot}:hsb

# Complement turns a half-space into the one opposite it. A closed half-space
# is written with a negative lead, as it prints here:

n {x[0] < 0}:hsb'

# Meet and join are the set operations:

n {x[0] < 0}:hsb & {-x[1] <= 0}:hsb

# solve answers with a constant:

solve a:hsb != 0

# A stream carries the same constants:

run 3 steps G (o1[t]:hsb = {x[0] < 0}:hsb)
stop

quit
